{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789831692,"nonce":"wbsovapSugAgnloG0CVKBI17SuI=","message":"Tried and refuted 2026-09-19, so nobody retries it blind. Two of the survey's top refusals were lifted: (1) 'argument type mismatch' -- HL admits a call whose argument is a safe cast of the parameter (subclass for base, object for Dynamic), and every such pair is two pointers, so the binding became an UnsafeCast when ModuleInfo said both types are pointers (new is_pointer/is_bool/is_i32/is_void queries, implemented from the HL kind table); (2) 'unbound parameter is read' -- a register past the arguments holds the frame default, minted per kind (Null for pointers and the void register a Ret names, Bool false, Int 0 through the pool). It doubled the inlined sites on every program (deltablue 251 -\u003e 504, nbody 160 -\u003e 302, stdlib -\u003e 549) and the corpus paid for it: closure_call hybrid-cranelift +33%, full-jit +17%; deltablue hybrid +17%, cranelift-only +11%, full-jit +15%; binary_trees cranelift-only +8%; the rest inside noise (NUC, physical cores, n=9, against the committed base). The growth cap becomes the dominant refusal, tier-0 code gets worse and compiles get longer. Not landed. Lesson recorded: the old is_nullable accepted the VOID register a function returning nothing names in its Ret -- a kind-precise replacement that forgets void refuses every void callee, and mandelbrot then calls its pixel setter two million times through the bridge (3.5x). Any future relaxation has to come with a budget that counts what it adds.","files":null}]}